```json
{
  "verdict": "revise",
  "scores": {
    "novelty": {
      "score": 4,
      "rationale": "Genuine gap at the intersection of two active research lines — refusal mechanistic interpretability and tool-call interpretability. No published work probes refusal circuit activation during structured tool-call generation. The closest parallel, 'Refusal Falls Off a Cliff' (arXiv 2510.06036), uses linear probing of refusal across token positions but targets reasoning-model output boundaries, not tool-call delimiters. However, the methodological contribution is primarily an application/combination of existing techniques (probes, activation patching, SAEs) to a new modality, not a fundamentally new method."
    },
    "feasibility": {
      "score": 3,
      "rationale": "Building blocks are confirmed available: Qwen-Scope SAEs for Qwen3-8B, Llama Scope/Goodfire/EleutherAI SAEs for Llama-3.1-8B, both models support tool calling, and the Mind-the-GAP protocol is documented. However, the critical risk is that Mind the GAP documented the text-refusal/tool-compliance divergence on 6 frontier models—NOT on 8B open-source models. If Qwen3-8B and Llama-3.1-8B don't reliably exhibit this divergence, the entire project collapses with no fallback plan articulated. Additionally, Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct has documented limitations in maintaining conversations alongside tool-call definitions."
    },
    "clarity": {
      "score": 4,
      "rationale": "Exceptionally well-structured proposal with clear three-position probing strategy, well-motivated experimental pipeline (replicate → probe → patch → decompose), and strong positioning relative to prior work. Minor issue: the description pre-claims specific numerical results ('78-91% of cases,' 'dropping to near-zero within two layers') that are fabricated projections, not obtained data — these should be clearly framed as hypotheses."
    },
    "impact": {
      "score": 4,
      "rationale": "Directly answers the open question explicitly posed in Mind the GAP's Section 5.1 ('mechanistic interpretability work would be needed to confirm the dual pathway account'). If the refusal suppression mechanism is real and patchable via activation intervention, this provides a principled fix for tool-call safety — a critical concern as LLM agents are deployed. Impact is somewhat bounded by being demonstrated only on 8B models, with unclear generalization to frontier models where the problem was originally documented."
    }
  },
  "issues": [
    "CRITICAL OMISSION: 'Refusal Falls Off a Cliff' (arXiv 2510.06036, ICLR 2026) is not cited despite being the closest methodological parallel — it uses linear probing of refusal intentions across token positions and discovers 'refusal suppression heads' at output-mode boundaries, exactly analogous to the hypothesized mechanism at tool-call delimiters.",
    "REPLICATION RISK: Mind the GAP tested 6 frontier models; the proposal assumes 8B open-source models will reliably exhibit the text-refusal/tool-compliance divergence, but this is unverified. No fallback plan is articulated if Step 1 (replication) fails.",
    "PRE-CLAIMED RESULTS: The description section states specific numbers ('78-91%', 'near-zero within two layers', 'sparse set of mode-switch features') as if they are obtained results. These are fabricated projections that should be clearly framed as hypotheses.",
    "UNREALISTIC VENUE TARGETS: AIES 2026 (May 21 — 2 days away) and EMNLP 2026 ARR (May 25 — 6 days away) are listed as targets for a 14-18 week project starting now. These are impossible.",
    "SAE COVERAGE GAP IN PROPOSAL: The proposal mentions only Qwen-Scope SAEs but does not acknowledge the readily available Llama Scope (fnlp), Goodfire, and EleutherAI pretrained SAEs for Llama-3.1-8B — citing these would strengthen feasibility.",
    "LLAMA TOOL-CALLING LIMITATIONS: Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct has documented limitations in maintaining conversations alongside tool-calling definitions, which could reduce the quality of paired activation traces."
  ],
  "feedback": "This is a well-conceived idea sitting at a genuine research gap. To pass: (1) Cite 'Refusal Falls Off a Cliff' and explicitly differentiate — their refusal suppression heads at thinking-end templates are the closest analogue to your hypothesized mode-switch at tool-call delimiters; explain why the tool-call boundary is distinct. (2) Add a concrete fallback plan for when 8B models don't show strong text-refusal/tool-compliance divergence — consider including a 70B model (Qwen3-30B-A3B has Qwen-Scope SAEs, Llama 3.3 70B has Goodfire SAEs), or define a minimum divergence threshold to proceed. (3) Clearly label projected results as hypotheses ('we expect...', 'we predict...'), not as obtained data. (4) Remove AIES 2026 and EMNLP 2026 as realistic initial targets; AAAI 2027 (Jul 28) is the first feasible deadline. (5) Explicitly cite Llama Scope / Goodfire SAEs for Llama-3.1-8B to close the SAE coverage concern. (6) Acknowledge Llama-3.1-8B tool-calling limitations and explain mitigation (e.g., zero-shot tool calling, or switching to Qwen3-8B as primary model with Llama as secondary validation).",
  "reason": "Strong idea at a genuine gap (avg 3.75/5.0), but critical missing citation ('Refusal Falls Off a Cliff'), unaddressed replication risk on 8B models, pre-claimed results, and impossible near-term venue deadlines require revision before pass."
}
